1
00:05:28,235 --> 00:05:34,235
When $100 million dollars goes missing, the hunter becomes the hunted.

2
00:10:56,470 --> 00:11:02,470
Kill Shot is a action film directed by Ari Novak.

3
00:16:24,705 --> 00:16:30,705
Posing as hunters, a group of terrorists are in search of $100 million that
was stolen and lost in a plane crash en route from Afghanistan.

4
00:21:52,941 --> 00:21:58,941
Jackson Hardison, played by Rib Hillis.

5
00:27:21,176 --> 00:27:27,176
Kate, played by Rachel Cook.

6
00:32:49,411 --> 00:32:55,411
Jim McCluskey, played by Todd Gordon.

7
00:38:17,647 --> 00:38:23,647
Alpha ONE, played by Ari Novak.

8
00:43:45,882 --> 00:43:51,882
Sarah Hardison, played by Xian Mikol.

9
00:49:14,117 --> 00:49:20,117
Dina Diablo, played by Mara Ohara.

10
00:54:42,352 --> 00:54:48,352
Kill is a 2023 Indian Hindi-language action film written and directed by Nikhil
Nagesh Bhat and produced by Dharma Productions and Sikhya Entertainment.

11
01:00:10,588 --> 01:00:16,588
The film, which is inspired by a train robbery experienced by Bhat in 1995, stars Lakshya,
Raghav Juyal, Ashish Vidyarthi, Harsh Chhaya, Tanya Maniktala and Abhishek Chauhan.

12
01:05:38,823 --> 01:05:44,823
Kill premiered at the Toronto International Film Festival on 7 September 2023, where it
was first runner-up for the People's Choice Award: Midnight Madness.

13
01:11:07,058 --> 01:11:13,058
It was also screened at the Tribeca Film Festival in June 2024.

14
01:16:35,294 --> 01:16:41,294
Kill was theatrically released on 5 July 2024 to positive reviews from critics, who praised its cinematrography, visuals,
soundtrack, cast performances and action sequences but criticised the overly graphic violence and plot.

15
01:22:03,529 --> 01:22:09,529
The film grossed ₹47.12 crore against a budget of ₹20 crore.

16
01:27:31,764 --> 01:27:37,764
Kill received fifteen nominations at the 70th Filmfare Awards including  Best Film, Best  Director (Bhat),
Best Male Debut (Lakshya) and Best Supporting Actor (Juyal) and won Best Male Debut (Lakshya).
